/-
Cereceda/Bip/Example8.lean — open problem 1 (short v3.90 l. 743-752): the 8-vertex instance where two moves per vertex fail.
Author: Dave Goel. Copyright (C) Dave Goel 2026--now.

ROUTE (a checked search; the paper cites [G, Remark 34.9] for this claim). A state is a colouring `c` and move counts `k`
(each at most 2). Along a sequence with at most two moves per vertex, every state is LIVE: a vertex that has made two
moves is already on its β colour (it never moves again). `certTree` lists the codes of the live states reachable from
(α, 0) (code = ∑ (c v + 4 k v) 12^v). The kernel checks (by `decide +kernel`, no native code): the start is listed,
every legal move from a listed state to a live state gives a listed state, and no listed state has the colouring β.
The induction `no_seq` turns this into: no sequence from α to β moves every vertex at most twice.
-/
import Cereceda.Defs.Example8
import Cereceda.Defs.Bipartite
import Cereceda.Setting.Small

namespace Cereceda

